# Workflow: Build > Execute Ticket (Dev Story)

<critical>You MUST only start with clean GIT status.</critical>
<critical>You MUST clarify ambiguous requirements BEFORE implementing.</critical>
<critical>You MUST log all issues/decisions in `### DEV AGENT RECORD`.</critical>
<critical>You MUST run all tests (Unit + E2E) before completing.</critical>
<critical>Read `~/.slopdog/plans/context.yaml` ONCE at start. Do NOT write to context.yaml unless updating ticket status/progress.</critical>
<critical>Detect or ask for OUTPUT MODE before Step 1. All outputs MUST conform to the detected mode format.</critical>

<variables>
  {{output_mode}} - Either "app" or "cli" (detected at Step 0)
  {{current_ticket}} - Read from context.yaml at Step 1
  {{ticket_path}} - Path to the active ticket markdown file
  {{git_status}} - Result of git status check
</variables>

<output-modes>
  ## Output Mode: app
  - **When**: Workflow executed directly in Cursor IDE
  - **Format**: Markdown with emoji indicators
  - **Audience**: Human user reading in IDE
  
  ## Output Mode: cli
  - **When**: Workflow called via `cursor-agent` CLI
  - **Format**: Structured XML for programmatic parsing
  - **Audience**: Webapp GUI rendering engine
  
  ## Mode Detection Rules
  1. If prompt contains `--mode=cli` or `[cli]` → cli mode
  2. If prompt contains `--mode=app` or `[app]` → app mode
  3. If environment variable `CURSOR_AGENT_CLI=true` → cli mode
  4. If ambiguous → Ask user to select mode before proceeding
  
  ## Thinking Output Guidelines (CLI Mode)
  Emit `<thinking>` outputs strategically - not for every micro-step:
  
  | EMIT thinking for | SKIP thinking for |
  |-------------------|-------------------|
  | Starting a new task | Trivial file reads |
  | Making non-obvious decisions | Standard operations |
  | Encountering ambiguity | Repetitive actions |
  | Finding unexpected code | Simple checks |
  | Changing implementation approach | Progress updates |
  
  **Frequency**: ~1-3 thinking outputs per task, more if complex decisions arise.
</output-modes>

<xml-schema>
  ## CLI Mode XML Output Schema
  
  All CLI mode outputs MUST conform to these XML structures:
  
  ### Step Status Output
  ```xml
  <workflow-output>
    <step number="N" goal="Step Goal Text">
      <status>complete|in_progress|blocked|failed</status>
      <checks>
        <check id="check-id" status="pass|fail">Description</check>
      </checks>
      <message>Human-readable summary</message>
      <next-step number="N+1" goal="Next Step Goal"/>
    </step>
  </workflow-output>
  ```
  
  ### Progress Update Output
  ```xml
  <workflow-output>
    <progress>
      <ticket id="{{current_ticket}}">
        <tasks completed="N" total="M"/>
        <acceptance-criteria completed="N" total="M"/>
        <current-task id="task-id">Task description</current-task>
      </ticket>
    </progress>
  </workflow-output>
  ```
  
  ### Action Log Output
  ```xml
  <workflow-output>
    <action-log>
      <entry type="plan|implement|decision|bug|ambiguity" timestamp="ISO8601">
        <description>What happened</description>
        <files>
          <file path="path/to/file" action="created|modified|deleted"/>
        </files>
      </entry>
    </action-log>
  </workflow-output>
  ```
  
  ### Completion Output
  ```xml
  <workflow-output>
    <completion>
      <ticket id="{{current_ticket}}" status="review">
        <progress percent="100"/>
        <tests status="pass|fail">
          <unit status="pass|fail" command="npm test"/>
          <e2e status="pass|fail" command="npm run e2e"/>
        </tests>
        <build status="pass|fail"/>
        <lint status="pass|fail"/>
        <summary>
          <po-summary>Summary for product owner</po-summary>
          <tech-summary>Summary for tech lead</tech-summary>
        </summary>
        <files-changed count="N">
          <file path="path/to/file"/>
        </files-changed>
      </ticket>
    </completion>
  </workflow-output>
  ```
  
  ### Question/Prompt Output (for user input)
  ```xml
  <workflow-output>
    <prompt type="confirmation|selection|input">
      <question>Question text</question>
      <options>
        <option id="opt-id" label="Option Label"/>
      </options>
      <default>default-option-id</default>
    </prompt>
  </workflow-output>
  ```
  
  ### Error/Halt Output
  ```xml
  <workflow-output>
    <error type="validation|git|test|build">
      <message>Error description</message>
      <action>Required action to resolve</action>
      <halt>true|false</halt>
    </error>
  </workflow-output>
  ```
  
  ### Thinking Output (Agent Reasoning)
  Use `<thinking>` to expose agent reasoning for UI display (e.g., collapsible panels, loading states).
  
  ```xml
  <workflow-output>
    <thinking step="N" phase="planning|analyzing|implementing|verifying">
      <context>What the agent is looking at</context>
      <reasoning>Chain of thought / analysis</reasoning>
      <hypothesis>What the agent believes or is testing</hypothesis>
      <decision>Conclusion reached (if any)</decision>
      <next-action>What the agent will do next</next-action>
    </thinking>
  </workflow-output>
  ```
  
  ### Thinking Phases
  | Phase | When Used |
  |-------|-----------|
  | `planning` | Reading task, determining approach |
  | `analyzing` | Examining code, understanding context |
  | `implementing` | Writing/editing code, making changes |
  | `verifying` | Running tests, checking results |
  
  ### Streaming Thinking (for live updates)
  For long operations, emit incremental thinking:
  
  ```xml
  <workflow-output>
    <thinking-stream step="N" phase="analyzing">
      <chunk seq="1">Reading ticket requirements...</chunk>
      <chunk seq="2">Found 3 unchecked tasks...</chunk>
      <chunk seq="3">First task maps to AC-1...</chunk>
    </thinking-stream>
  </workflow-output>
  ```
  
  ### Observation Output (intermediate findings)
  ```xml
  <workflow-output>
    <observation type="code|test|file|dependency">
      <target>What was examined (file path, test name, etc.)</target>
      <finding>What was discovered</finding>
      <relevance>high|medium|low</relevance>
      <affects>Which task/AC this impacts</affects>
    </observation>
  </workflow-output>
  ```
</xml-schema>

<workflow>

<step n="0" goal="Mode Detection">
  <action>
    **Detect Output Mode**:
    - Check initial prompt for explicit mode indicator:
      - `--mode=cli` or `[cli]` → Set {{output_mode}} = "cli"
      - `--mode=app` or `[app]` → Set {{output_mode}} = "app"
    - Check for environment context (cursor-agent CLI typically sets context)
    - If mode cannot be determined, ask user:
      
      **app mode**: "Which output mode? (app = Cursor IDE, cli = cursor-agent webapp)"
      
      **cli mode**:
      ```xml
      <workflow-output>
        <prompt type="selection">
          <question>Select output mode for this workflow</question>
          <options>
            <option id="app" label="App Mode - Cursor IDE (markdown + emoji)"/>
            <option id="cli" label="CLI Mode - cursor-agent webapp (structured XML)"/>
          </options>
          <default>app</default>
        </prompt>
      </workflow-output>
      ```
  </action>

  <output mode="app">
    ✅ **Mode Detected**: {{output_mode}}
    
    ➡️ **Beginning Step 1: Context Loading & Validation**
  </output>

  <output mode="cli">
    ```xml
    <workflow-output>
      <step number="0" goal="Mode Detection">
        <status>complete</status>
        <checks>
          <check id="mode-detected" status="pass">Output mode: {{output_mode}}</check>
        </checks>
        <next-step number="1" goal="Context Loading &amp; Validation"/>
      </step>
    </workflow-output>
    ```
  </output>
</step>

<step n="1" goal="Context Loading & Validation">
  <action>
    **Check Git Status**:
    - Must be clean. If not, HALT.
    - Report: `[ ✅ | ❌ ] Git Status Clean`
  </action>

  <action>
    **Load Ticket**:
    - Ask user to select ticket (if not current).
    - Update `~/.slopdog/plans/context.yaml` (`current_ticket`, `status: In Progress`).
    - Report: `[ ✅ | ❌ ] Ticket Loaded: {{current_ticket}}`
  </action>

  <action>
    **Validate Readiness**:
    - Mode must be `build` or `task`.
    - First unchecked task must exist.
    - Tasks must map to ACs: `(AC: AC-#...)`.
    - Report: `[ ✅ | ❌ ] Ticket Validated for Execution`
  </action>

  <check if="not ready">
    <critical>STOP. Ticket not ready or invalid mode.</critical>
    <action>Fix ticket or switch mode.</action>
    
    <error-output mode="app">
      ❌ **HALT**: Ticket not ready or invalid mode.
      **Action Required**: Fix ticket or switch to build/task mode.
    </error-output>
    
    <error-output mode="cli">
      ```xml
      <workflow-output>
        <error type="validation">
          <message>Ticket not ready or invalid mode</message>
          <action>Fix ticket or switch to build/task mode</action>
          <halt>true</halt>
        </error>
      </workflow-output>
      ```
    </error-output>
  </check>

  <output mode="app">
    ✅ **Ending Step 1: Context Loading & Validation**
    [ ✅ ] Git Status Clean
    [ ✅ ] Ticket Loaded: {{current_ticket}}
    [ ✅ ] Ticket Validated for Execution
    
    ➡️ **Beginning Step 2: Execution Loop (Plan -> Implement -> Mark)**
  </output>

  <output mode="cli">
    ```xml
    <workflow-output>
      <step number="1" goal="Context Loading &amp; Validation">
        <status>complete</status>
        <checks>
          <check id="git-status" status="pass">Git status clean</check>
          <check id="ticket-loaded" status="pass">Ticket loaded: {{current_ticket}}</check>
          <check id="ticket-validated" status="pass">Ticket validated for execution</check>
        </checks>
        <message>Context loaded and validated successfully</message>
        <next-step number="2" goal="Execution Loop (Plan -> Implement -> Mark)"/>
      </step>
    </workflow-output>
    ```
  </output>
</step>

<step n="2" goal="Execution Loop (Plan -> Implement -> Mark)">
  <action>
    **Loop until all tasks [x]:**
    
    **A. Plan**:
    - Read current unchecked task.
    - Write 1-line plan in `### DEV AGENT RECORD`.
    
    **B. Implement**:
    - Write/Edit code.
    - **Log immediately**:
      - `- [Time] [Spec ambiguity] ...`
      - `- [Time] [Bug] ...`
      - `- [Time] [Decision] ...`
    
    **C. Mark**:
    - Check `[x]` task.
    - **Sync ACs**: If all tasks for an AC are done, check `[x]` the corresponding AC in `## Acceptance Criteria`.
    - Add files to `### File List`.
    
    **D. Update Progress**:
    - Update ticket YAML `facets.progress` (e.g., `completed: x`, `total: y`).
    
    **E. Check Next**:
    - If more tasks, repeat A.
  </action>

  <loop-iteration-output mode="app">
    📋 **Task**: [Task description]
    🔧 **Plan**: [1-line implementation plan]
    ⏳ **Implementing...**
    
    ---
    ✅ **Task Complete**: [Task description]
    📁 **Files Modified**: [file1.ts, file2.ts]
    📊 **Progress**: [N/M] tasks | [X/Y] ACs
  </loop-iteration-output>

  <loop-iteration-output mode="cli">
    ```xml
    <workflow-output>
      <progress>
        <ticket id="{{current_ticket}}">
          <tasks completed="N" total="M"/>
          <acceptance-criteria completed="X" total="Y"/>
          <current-task id="task-id">Task description</current-task>
        </ticket>
      </progress>
      <action-log>
        <entry type="plan" timestamp="2025-01-28T10:30:00Z">
          <description>1-line implementation plan</description>
        </entry>
        <entry type="implement" timestamp="2025-01-28T10:35:00Z">
          <description>Task completed</description>
          <files>
            <file path="src/file1.ts" action="modified"/>
            <file path="src/file2.ts" action="created"/>
          </files>
        </entry>
      </action-log>
    </workflow-output>
    ```
  </loop-iteration-output>

  <decision-log-output mode="app">
    📝 **Log Entry**: `[Time] [Type] Description`
  </decision-log-output>

  <decision-log-output mode="cli">
    ```xml
    <workflow-output>
      <action-log>
        <entry type="decision|bug|ambiguity" timestamp="ISO8601">
          <description>What was decided/found</description>
        </entry>
      </action-log>
    </workflow-output>
    ```
  </decision-log-output>

  <thinking-output mode="app">
    💭 **Thinking**: [Brief reasoning shown inline or omitted]
  </thinking-output>

  <thinking-output mode="cli">
    ```xml
    <workflow-output>
      <thinking step="2" phase="planning">
        <context>Reading task: "Add input validation to form component"</context>
        <reasoning>This task requires modifying the form component to validate user input before submission. Need to check existing validation patterns in codebase.</reasoning>
        <hypothesis>Existing validation utils in src/utils/validation.ts can be reused</hypothesis>
        <next-action>Read current form component and validation utils</next-action>
      </thinking>
    </workflow-output>
    ```
    
    ```xml
    <workflow-output>
      <thinking step="2" phase="analyzing">
        <context>Examining src/components/Form.tsx</context>
        <reasoning>Form currently submits without validation. Found handleSubmit at line 45. Validation utils export validateEmail, validateRequired.</reasoning>
        <decision>Will add validation call before form submission using existing utils</decision>
        <next-action>Implement validation in handleSubmit function</next-action>
      </thinking>
    </workflow-output>
    ```
    
    ```xml
    <workflow-output>
      <observation type="code">
        <target>src/components/Form.tsx:45-60</target>
        <finding>handleSubmit has no input validation, directly calls API</finding>
        <relevance>high</relevance>
        <affects>Task 1 (AC: AC-1)</affects>
      </observation>
    </workflow-output>
    ```
  </thinking-output>
</step>

<step n="3" goal="Completion & Verification">
  <action>
    **Verify Acceptance Criteria**:
    - Review `## Acceptance Criteria`. Are they met?
    - Report: `[ ✅ | ❌ ] All ACs Met`
  </action>

  <action>
    **Run All Tests**:
    - Unit (Vitest): Record command + pass/fail + artifact link.
    - E2E (Playwright): Record command + pass/fail + artifact link.
    - **Console/Runtime Check**: Verify no console errors or runtime crashes during basic smoke tests.
    - Report: `[ ✅ | ❌ ] Tests Passed (Unit + E2E + Console)`
  </action>

  <check if="tests failed">
    <critical>Cannot complete ticket with failing tests.</critical>
    <action>Fix regressions before proceeding.</action>
    
    <error-output mode="app">
      ❌ **Tests Failed**: Cannot complete ticket with failing tests.
      **Action Required**: Fix regressions before proceeding.
    </error-output>
    
    <error-output mode="cli">
      ```xml
      <workflow-output>
        <error type="test">
          <message>Tests failed - cannot complete ticket</message>
          <action>Fix regressions before proceeding</action>
          <halt>true</halt>
          <details>
            <unit status="fail" output="Test output here"/>
            <e2e status="fail" output="E2E output here"/>
          </details>
        </error>
      </workflow-output>
      ```
    </error-output>
  </check>

  <action>
    **Run Build & Lint**:
    - Ensure clean build.
    - Report: `[ ✅ | ❌ ] Build & Lint Clean`
  </action>

  <action>
    **Taxonomy Drift Check**:
    - If docs touched, check `docs/taxonomy.yaml` for new tags.
  </action>

  <output mode="app">
    ✅ **Ending Step 3: Completion & Verification**
    [ ✅ ] All ACs Met
    [ ✅ ] Tests Passed (Unit + E2E)
    [ ✅ ] Build & Lint Clean
    
    ➡️ **Beginning Step 4: Handoff**
  </output>

  <output mode="cli">
    ```xml
    <workflow-output>
      <step number="3" goal="Completion &amp; Verification">
        <status>complete</status>
        <checks>
          <check id="acs-met" status="pass">All acceptance criteria met</check>
          <check id="tests-unit" status="pass">Unit tests passed</check>
          <check id="tests-e2e" status="pass">E2E tests passed</check>
          <check id="build" status="pass">Build successful</check>
          <check id="lint" status="pass">Lint clean</check>
        </checks>
        <tests status="pass">
          <unit status="pass" command="npm run test"/>
          <e2e status="pass" command="npm run e2e"/>
        </tests>
        <build status="pass"/>
        <lint status="pass"/>
        <next-step number="4" goal="Handoff"/>
      </step>
    </workflow-output>
    ```
  </output>
</step>

<step n="4" goal="Handoff">
  <action>
    **Update Ticket**:
    - Status: `Review`.
    - **Final Sync**: Ensure all ACs and Tasks are `[x]`.
    - **Progress Metadata**: Set `facets.progress.completed` to equal `total`.
    - Add `### Completion Notes` to `## Dev Agent Record`.
    - Include: PO Summary, Tech Lead Summary, Evidence Links.
    - Report: `[ ✅ | ❌ ] Ticket Updated to Review`
  </action>

  <output mode="app">
    ### Execution Complete
    - **Ticket**: [Link]
    - **Status**: [ ✅ ] Review
    - **Progress**: [ ✅ ] 100% [xxxxxxxxxx]
    - **Tests**: [ ✅ ] Passed (Evidence Attached)
    - **Ready for**: Code Review
  </output>

  <output mode="cli">
    ```xml
    <workflow-output>
      <completion>
        <ticket id="{{current_ticket}}" status="review">
          <progress percent="100"/>
          <tests status="pass">
            <unit status="pass" command="npm run test"/>
            <e2e status="pass" command="npm run e2e"/>
          </tests>
          <build status="pass"/>
          <lint status="pass"/>
          <summary>
            <po-summary>Brief summary of what was implemented for product owner</po-summary>
            <tech-summary>Technical implementation details for tech lead</tech-summary>
          </summary>
          <files-changed count="N">
            <file path="src/feature/component.ts"/>
            <file path="src/feature/component.test.ts"/>
          </files-changed>
          <ready-for>Code Review</ready-for>
        </ticket>
      </completion>
    </workflow-output>
    ```
  </output>
</step>

</workflow>
